# Obsidian vault is the shared memory (Sean, 2026-11-02)

Design source of truth and shared record for Cursor and Claude: `C:\Users\Sean\Documents\GameDev` (Obsidian vault; Obsidian MCP via Local REST API, see `docs/CLAUDE_CODE_MCP.md`). If the repo disagrees with the vault on design, the vault wins.

Before working: read `Projects/Four-in-a-Rogue/Design/vertical-slice-v0.1.md` and the latest notes in `Projects/Four-in-a-Rogue/Session-Logs/` and `Decisions/Decision-Log.md`.

Always store your work in the vault, during the session (not only in chat or code):

- **Session summary** (what was done, branch/state, open items): `Projects/Four-in-a-Rogue/Session-Logs/YYYY-MM-DD Cursor - <topic>.md`, frontmatter `type: session`.
- **Decisions Sean makes**: append a row to `Projects/Four-in-a-Rogue/Decisions/Decision-Log.md`; if a rule changed, also update `Design/vertical-slice-v0.1.md` (or `GDD.md`) and repo `CLAUDE.md` §Locked rules.
- **Research / findings / reports**: `Projects/Four-in-a-Rogue/Research/<title>.md`, frontmatter `type: note`.
- Link new notes from `Projects/Four-in-a-Rogue/Four-in-a-Rogue.md`.

Follow the vault's `CLAUDE.md` for frontmatter and conventions.
